Two Loom AIE2P array fixes for the gate placement that frees the gate column's fill (yah gen_npu_gemm gwest):
- A worker channel to the sender's east neighbor (same row) is neighbor memory: the receiver loads the sender's
  memory through its west window, as vertical neighbors do through north / south. It was routed as a DMA stream.
- An intake multicast's members may have rings of different depth (one filler's compact single-record raw ring, the
  other's two records). The shared stage ring has the source member's depth; a deeper member's drain indexed stage
  records past it (another buffer: its decoder read garbage for every other raw record). A member's drain chain now
  covers both depths and takes the stage records in turn. Equal depths (every earlier image) are byte-identical.
diff --git a/loom/src/loom/target/arch/amd/xdna/aie2p/array/topology.c b/loom/src/loom/target/arch/amd/xdna/aie2p/array/topology.c
--- a/loom/src/loom/target/arch/amd/xdna/aie2p/array/topology.c
+++ b/loom/src/loom/target/arch/amd/xdna/aie2p/array/topology.c
@@ -1129,8 +1129,14 @@
